# flashmon configuration — copy this to `flashmon.yaml` (which is gitignored) and
# make it yours. flashmon is a generic installer; this file is the ONLY thing
# that brands it and lists its images, so each deployment ships its own and
# nothing here needs to be committed upstream.
#
#   project:  the brand shown throughout the UI. Every place the tool would say
#             its own name ("<project> Flasher", the flash button, the default
#             device hostname) uses this, so your deployment reads as its own
#             product rather than "flashmon". Also names the branded terminal
#             flasher `make` produces: <project>-flashmon (+ .zip).
#   url:      where THIS deployment is served. `make` bakes it into the branded
#             flashmon.py so a downloaded copy knows where to fetch config +
#             images from. Omit for a purely local/bundled setup.
#   builds:   the catalogue of ready-to-flash images. Each entry is:
#               name        the image name, and its distribution identity — the
#                           device reports it back as sys.build.dist, so a
#                           re-flash offer can mean "same dist, newer stamp".
#                           Free-format: a board may have several entries that
#                           differ in what is left out to fit its flash. Name it
#                           after the hw-<straddle> the detector reports so the
#                           browser can match a detected board to its image;
#                           `generic` is the fallback for any board without a
#                           dedicated image.
#               invocation  the `spangap build` arguments that produce it.
#               image       optional. A photo of the board, shown in the device
#                           box when a detection run identifies it: a path in the
#                           web root (devices/<board>.jpg by convention — see
#                           devices/README.md), never a remote URL. Left out, or
#                           pointing at a file that isn't there, the box is
#                           simply text-only.
#               version     DO NOT hand-edit. `make` in builds/ writes this per
#                           entry — the build datetime it stamped that image with
#                           — and names the image builds/<slug>_<name>_<version>.zip.
#                           A subset build re-stamps only the entries it rebuilt.
#                           It is the ordering field: a sortable stamp, which is
#                           why identity lives in `name` and not here.
#               flash_floor_kb  DO NOT hand-edit. Written by `make`: the minimum
#                           chip size this image needs. A board smaller than this
#                           cannot run it, and saying so here is what avoids a
#                           multi-megabyte download to discover it.
#               image_bytes DO NOT hand-edit. Written by `make`: the bytes this
#                           image writes to flash.
#             The browser (and flashmon.py) fetch that stamped image for the
#             detected board, falling back to builds/generic.zip.
#
# The browser prefers flashmon.local.yaml over flashmon.yaml when present, so you
# can override branding/catalogue per-machine without touching your own file.
#
# Order matters for `make`: each build rewrites the workspace's remembered target
# (.spangap-build), so the LAST entry is what a later bare `spangap build`
# resolves to.
project: MyProject
url: https://myproject.example/flashmon/
builds:
  - name: hw-lilygo-tdeck
    image: devices/hw-lilygo-tdeck.jpg
    invocation: myorg/myproject --with spangap/hw-lilygo-tdeck
  - name: generic
    invocation: myorg/myproject
